WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
WeGen2. Native pixel-space multimodal creation. An idea. A world of possibilities.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Reference-conditioned editing: change the green mountain city into a winter landscape.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
A handcrafted paper world is edited into an illuminated night scene.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Photographic detail: a portrait in the rain, with close-ups of lighting and materials.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
An illustrated fantasy film poster with model-generated lettering.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.000
A WeGen2 creation-studio poster with Chinese headlines, descriptive text, and six miniature scenes, generated together from one text prompt.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:38.000
A source person and eight garment and accessory references. The references form a contact sheet, then move beside the generated outfit.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:49.000
The generated outfit appears. Highlighted regions link to the blazer, shirt, jeans, sneakers, bag, belt and necklace references.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Successive image editing: add a reply to a fictional chat, then revise the messages.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
A cake-making comic: eight sequentially generated panels presented together on one canvas.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Behind every image, one connected model.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Native pixels: learned patch modules connect RGB images and the backbone. No separate pretrained vision encoder or latent autoencoder is used at inference.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:20.000
A-MoT: separate understanding and generation branches communicate through joint attention. Image and timestep residual pathways are part of the generation branch.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:29.000
A-MoE: three colored tokens all pass through the shared expert, while the router selects different expert subsets. Matching colored flows trace each token. Expert count is schematic.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:36.000
PHT: Progressive Heterogeneous Training. Alignment connects text, visual and multimodal learning, from 256 to 512 resolution.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.000
Creation adds multi-reference composition and variable aspect ratios, initially at a 512² pixel budget.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Creation increases the image pixel budget to 1024².

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:52.000
WeGen2: 61B total parameters, approximately 7B activated per generation token. Explore the project page.
